  - model-calibration
  - wesad
abstract: >-
  CalmSense compares four feature-based classifiers and a 1D convolutional neural
  network on WESAD using leave-one-subject-out evaluation. It processes ECG, EDA,
  temperature, respiration, and motion signals. The project also evaluates
  probability calibration, personalization, chest and wrist recordings, and
  transfer to the PhysioNet Non-EEG dataset. A static dashboard displays saved
  results and recorded signal excerpts.
